## 5. Competitor URL Analysis & Factual Verification

### Competitor Analysis ([CaratLane Men's Kada](https://www.caratlane.com/jewellery/mens+kada.html))
- **Structure:** CaratLane's URL is a commercial category listing with an SEO text footer covering generic gold kadas for men, traditional vs modern styles, Punjabi kada cultural significance, and basic sizing.
- **Key Competitor Omissions:** CaratLane targets only generic solid gold kadas and omits all education on **gold-plated** alternatives, electroplating microns, base metal reactions, and the "1 gram gold" myth.
- **BlueStone Differentiation:** Our article provides complete consumer transparency: acknowledging why men look for plated kadas, providing honest chemical and metallurgical explanations of plating degradation, and showing why upgrading to BIS-hallmarked solid gold offers superior dermatological comfort, structural permanence, and generational value.

### Factual Sources & Standards Cited
- **Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS):** Mandatory hallmarking with tripartite marks (triangular BIS stamp, purity grade `22K916` / `18K750`, and unique 6-digit alphanumeric HUID code verifiable on the BIS Care App). Clarified that plated/costume jewellery cannot legally receive BIS hallmarking.
- **World Gold Council (WGC):** Gold purity fineness scales (22Kt = 91.6% pure gold; 18Kt = 75.0% pure gold) and metallurgical alloy hardening principles.
- **Dermatological Health Science:** Copper/brass oxidation mechanisms with perspiration (lactic acid and sodium chloride forming copper carbonate/chloride) and nickel contact dermatitis risks.
- **Taxation:** Current 3% Goods and Services Tax (GST) applied to precious metal value and craftsmanship charges in India.

